# AppHost C# Rules

## var Usage

In AppHost, `var` is accepted and can be used for local declarations. This exception applies only to the AppHost project.

```csharp
// ✅ Acceptable in AppHost
var builder = DistributedApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
var apiService = builder.AddProject<ProjectReference>("apiservice", "../MyPcBuild.ApiService/MyPcBuild.ApiService.csproj");
```

## Otherwise

Follow general C# best practices. C# 14 features (collection expressions, target-typed new, etc.) are still encouraged where they improve readability.
